nodecode-android-emulator is a rewrite of PIR8-Software's PIR8-Software/hermes-android-emulator:

  https://github.com/PIR8-Software/hermes-android-emulator
  commit 3b5cb61e8bd6c4600f797a44c44234a6371bd59a
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Roy Crabtree (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's eighteen model-facing tools — emu_status, emu_shell,
emu_install, emu_uninstall, emu_screenshot, emu_tap, emu_swipe, emu_type,
emu_key, emu_launch, emu_packages, emu_push, emu_pull, emu_logcat, emu_gps,
emu_battery, emu_network and emu_deeplink — with their argument names and
their answer shapes; the serial guard that pins every call to an emulator and
refuses a non-emulator serial without a deliberate opt-in; the input checks
(package, activity, keycode, URL, remote path, logcat filter) and the escaping
of typed text and shell words; the host-write confinement to the home, the cwd
and the temp dir with no silent overwrite; and the resource bounds on timeouts,
line counts and output size. The Python (subprocess, shlex, pathlib) is Common
Lisp here: nlk:run-bounded starts adb, one section declaration states the
settings, and eighteen nlk:define-contract declarations state the tools'
arguments, so the schema the model is shown and the body that runs are one
shape. The one seam, NODECODE-ANDROID-EMULATOR::*RUN*, is what a test stubs.

Left out: everything of the plugin that is not a model-facing tool — the
Hermes dashboard API (start/stop, AVD create/list/wipe/delete, sdkmanager
system-image installs, screen recording, touch record-and-replay, the
instrumented-test runner, push notifications), the desktop sidebar with its
live screen and keyboard shortcuts, and the emu start/stop/status CLI wrapper.
Those are surfaces of the Hermes gateway and desktop, and a cell's equivalent
would be a chat lane or a page rather than the tools this rewrite keeps. The
host-write check is also said differently: the original resolved symlinks and
compared real paths, while the cell refuses a ".." segment and compares the
written path against the allowed roots.
